 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (RTA), a clause permitting the landlord to enter the unit at any time and for any reason without notice is void and unenforceable. Section 25 establishes that a landlord may only enter a rental unit in accordance with sections 26 (entry without notice under narrow, specified conditions, such as emergencies) or 27 (entry with 24 hours written notice for specific permitted purposes). Furthermore, under subsection 4(1) of the RTA, any lease provision that conflicts with the Act is void.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 25",
